The first function should take an array of entities and return an arraybuffer. The second function should take an arraybuffer and return an array of entities.

```javascript
function packEntities(entities) {
    let buffer = new ArrayBuffer(entities.length * 8);
    let view = new DataView(buffer);
    for (let i = 0; i < entities.length; i++) {
        let entity = entities[i];
        view.setUint8(i * 8, entity.id & 0x0F);
        view.setUint8(i * 8 + 1, (entity.size & 0x07) << 4);
        view.setUint8(i * 8 + 2, (entity.size & 0x38) >> 3);
        view.setUint8(i * 8 + 3, (entity.size & 0xC0) >> 6);
        view.setUint8(i * 8 + 4, (entity.id & 0xF0) >> 4);
        view.setUint8(i * 8 + 5, (entity.id & 0xFF00) >> 8);
        view.setUint8(i * 8 + 6, (entity.id & 0xFF0000) >> 16);
        view.setUint8(i * 8 + 7, (entity.id & 0xFF000000) >> 24);
    }
    return buffer;
}

function unpackEntities(buffer) {
    let view = new DataView(buffer);
    let entities = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < buffer.byteLength / 8; i++) {
        let entity = {
            id: (view.getUint8(i * 8) | (view.getUint8(i * 8 + 1) << 4) | (view.getUint8(i * 8 + 2) << 8) | (view.getUint8(i * 8 + 3) << 12)) & 0xFF,
            size: (view.getUint8(i * 8 + 4) | (view.getUint8(i * 8 + 5) << 4) | (view.getUint8(i * 8 + 6) << 8) | (view.getUint8(i * 8 + 7) << 12)) & 0x38
        };
        entities.push(entity);
    }
    return entities;
}
```

The above code is a solution to the problem. It defines two functions, `packEntities` and `unpackEntities`, which pack and unpack an array of entities to an arraybuffer and vice versa. The entities have 4-bit id and 3-bit size fields, and there is no padding between entities or their fields. The packing and unpacking are done in little-endian byte order. The `packEntities` function takes an array of entities, creates an arraybuffer with a size of `entities.length * 8`, and uses a DataView to set the values of the entities in the arraybuffer. The `unpackEntities` function takes an arraybuffer, creates a DataView, and uses it to get the values of the entities from the arraybuffer. The entities are then pushed into an array and returned. 

