You can create a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image by following these steps:

1. Create a new PHP file in the `wp-content/plugins` directory of your WordPress installation. For example, you can name it `custom-block.php`.
2. In this file, add the following code to register the block:
```php
<?php
/*
Plugin Name: Custom Block
Description: A custom block with a heading, paragraph, and image.
*/

function register_custom_block() {
    wp_register_block_type(
        'custom-block/block',
        array(
            'title' => __( 'Custom Block' ),
            'description' => __( 'A custom block with a heading, paragraph, and image.' ),
            'render_callback' => 'render_custom_block',
        )
    );
}
add_action( 'init', 'register_custom_block' );
```
This code registers a new block type called `custom-block/block` with a title, description, and a render callback function called `render_custom_block`.

3. Create a new PHP file in the same directory as the previous file, for example, `custom-block-render.php`. In this file, add the following code to define the render callback function:
```php
<?php
function render_custom_block( $attributes, $content, $block ) {
    $heading = $attributes['heading'];
    $paragraph = $attributes['paragraph'];
    $image_url = $attributes['image'];

    $html = '<div class="custom-block">';
    $html .= '<h2>' . $heading . '</h2>';
    $html .= '<p>' . $paragraph . '</p>';
    $html .= '<img src="' . $image_url . '" alt="Image">';
    $html .= '</div>';

    return $html;
}
```
This code defines the render callback function `render_custom_block` which takes three arguments: `$attributes`, `$content`, and `$block`. It extracts the heading, paragraph, and image URL from the block attributes and uses them to generate the HTML for the block.

4. In the `custom-block.php` file, add the following code to enqueue the block's CSS and JavaScript files:
```php
function enqueue_custom_block_assets() {
    wp_enqueue_style( 'custom-block-style', plugins_url( 'css/custom-block.css', __FILE__ ) );
    wp_enqueue_script( 'custom-block-script', plugins_url( 'js/custom-block.js', __FILE__ ) );
}
add_action( 'enqueue_block_editor_assets', 'enqueue_custom_block_assets' );
```
This code enqueues two files: `custom-block.css` and `custom-block.js`. You can add your custom CSS and JavaScript code to these files.

5. Create the `custom-block.css` file in the same directory as the `custom-block.php` file and add your custom CSS code to it.

6. Create the `custom-block.js` file in the same directory as the `custom-block.php` file and add your custom JavaScript code to it.

7. Go to the WordPress block editor and click on the "+" icon to add a new block. Search for "Custom Block" and select it. You should see a new block with a heading, paragraph, and image.

That's it! You have now created a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image.

Note: This is a basic example and you can customize the block to fit your needs. You can also add more features, such as dynamic data, API calls, and more. 

Also, you can use the `wp.blocks.registerBlockType` function to register the block, instead of `wp_register_block_type`. The `wp.blocks.registerBlockType` function is the recommended way to register blocks in WordPress 5.


